WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.080
Game of Thrones fans can attest to a big truth:
if you don't pay close enough attention to

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:07.460
what's happening on screen, you'll miss out
on a ton of ton of tiny details.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:11.100
This certainly applied to the first episode
of Thrones' eighth and final season.

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:14.700
The premiere featured plenty of buzz-worthy
moments — like the heartwarming reunion

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:19.280
between Jon and Arya, the awkward reunion
between Jon and Bran, the dramatic reunion

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:23.710
between Bran and Jaime Lannister, plus that
dragon joyride and Jon discovering he's a

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:28.090
Targaryen and Daenerys not giving a single
hoot about telling Sam she burnt his family

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:28.580
alive.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:32.260
"Least I'll be allowed home again, now that
my brother's the lord"

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:39.400
What has people talking even more than all
that are the two blink-and-you'll-miss-them

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:43.280
cameos that most people didn't pick up on
the first time around — you know, on account

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:45.040
of everything else happening during the episode.

00:00:45.269 --> 00:00:49.780
In the season 8 premiere, there's a scene
in which Theon Greyjoy storms his uncle Euron's

00:00:49.789 --> 00:00:54.069
ship, making his way to his sister Yara, Before
he can rescue her, however, Theon has to pick

00:00:54.069 --> 00:00:55.800
off a few members of Euron's fleet.

00:00:55.840 --> 00:01:00.359
Theon's hand is steady as he fires an arrow
clean into the back of one man's skull, sending

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.540
it shooting out his eye.

00:01:01.769 --> 00:01:05.620
He and two men behind him put several more
arrows through the heads of other random guys

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:06.160
on deck.

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:10.920
The siege is successful, the path to Yara
is clear, and Theon is free to return to Winterfell

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:14.720
while Yara looks over the Ironborn as Queen
of the Iron Islands.

00:01:14.909 --> 00:01:18.760
On the surface, the scene doesn't seem out
of the ordinary: it's a calculated act of

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:20.969
violence executed to meet an end goal.

00:01:20.969 --> 00:01:24.939
Look closer at the people playing Theon's
victims, though, and you'll see that the sequence

00:01:24.939 --> 00:01:29.070
is anything but normal, as it features cameo
appearances from It's Always Sunny in Philadelphia

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:32.320
actor Rob McElhenney and Silicon Valley star
Martin Starr.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:33.760
"They gouged my eye out.

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:36.060
They gouged my f------ eye out."

00:01:36.079 --> 00:01:39.229
They aren't on screen for very long and the
dim lighting makes it difficult to recognize

00:01:39.229 --> 00:01:44.119
their faces, so it's easy to see why so many
never caught McElhenney and Starr on the season

00:01:44.119 --> 00:01:45.580
8 premiere of Game of Thrones.

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:51.659
Well they'll be cutting from your face to
his face, then back to your face, and then

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:52.920
we'll get to see his face again."

00:01:53.609 --> 00:01:57.440
With each passing season, the series has gotten
better at sneaking in celebrity cameos that

00:01:57.440 --> 00:01:59.960
only the most eagle-eyed viewers can immediately
find.

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:03.439
Over the years, Game of Thrones showrunners
David Benioff and D.B. Weiss

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:07.080
have managed to include musicians,
other actors, and even political figures on

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:07.580
the series.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:11.400
Even Weiss and Benioff themselves made cameo
appearances, their mugs seen in the Hall of

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.140
Faces at the House of Black and White.

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:17.320
And very few could forget the time singer-songwriter
Ed Sheeran appeared on Thrones, playing a

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:21.300
singing Lannister bannerman Arya met as she
was traveling to King's Landing.

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:25.680
While many Game of Thrones fans weren't keen
on Sheeran's cameo, most everyone is loving

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:29.960
that McElhenney and Starr got to be a part
of the series, if only for a few seconds each.

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:34.540
In a way, it marks a full-circle moment: McElhenney
is close friends with Benioff and Weiss, who

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:38.750
previously wrote the season 9 It's Always
Sunny episode "Flowers for Charlie" and made

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:42.780
their own small appearances on the season
12 installment "The Gang Goes to a Water Park."

00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:46.800
A longtime Thrones fan, McElhenney was thought
to have already cameoed on the show back in

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:51.640
season 6, appearing alongside his Always Sunny
co-star Charlie Day as Unsullied soldiers,

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:53.510
but that ended up just a rumor.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:56.080
"You're like what's that rascal Charlie up
to now?

00:02:56.090 --> 00:02:57.100
What's he up to this time?

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:58.080
I'm not thinking that at all."

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:02.140
Unfortunately, there's one person who definitely
won't appear on the final season of Game of

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:05.400
Thrones: the mastermind behind the whole thing,
George R.R. Martin.

00:03:05.710 --> 00:03:10.220
As it turns out, the A Song of Ice and Fire
author had the opportunity to cameo on season

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:14.600
8, but turned it down in favor of working
on finishing The Winds of Winter, the long-awaited

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:17.960
sixth book in his novel series upon which
the show is based.

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:22.160
In the game of Thrones cameos, you either
accept and play a character who probably dies,

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:24.790
or you decline and deliver on your past promises.

00:03:24.790 --> 00:03:28.540
McElhenney and Starr may have had more fun,
but Martin chose wisely.

